    {
      "id": "KriTRZw9DVDbu4uijdRI_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 31997.120315069955,
      "y": 4976.209107293374,
      "width": 785.4457588176839,
      "height": 544.3724432648355,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "e9pnScmRsSq_MUGJpNfyG"
      ],
      "frameId": "nmdQ86d6GcWHU9s4PiMlj",
      "index": "bD4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1357530400,
      "version": 1284,
      "versionNonce": 197402912,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764511352212,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "+ Data Abstraction - collection of data\nthat describes a data object. \n\n+ Procedural Abstraction - Sequence of\ninstructions that have a specific and\nlimited function.\n\n+ Control Abstraction - program control\nmechanism without specifying internal\ndetail. Eg: synchronization semaphore\nused to coordinate all activities in OS",
      "fontSize": 39.59072314653349,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "+ Data Abstraction - collection of data that describes a data object. \n\n+ Procedural Abstraction - Sequence of instructions that have a specific and limited function.\n\n+ Control Abstraction - program control mechanism without specifying internal detail. Eg: synchronization semaphore\nused to coordinate all activities in OS",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "arjcTZywFRTA0A3sML-zw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 32973.200185512425,
      "y": 4902.110542124906,
      "width": 947.2746222068865,
      "height": 708.8489527329689,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "e9pnScmRsSq_MUGJpNfyG"
      ],
      "frameId": "nmdQ86d6GcWHU9s4PiMlj",
      "index": "bD5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2110138656,
      "version": 1115,
      "versionNonce": 451018976,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "T6TaOKGNuTJyaSBw1honw",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1764511352212,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "+ Structural models - how the system is organized\ninto components.\n\n+ Framework models - identify reusable\narchitectural patterns common in similar\napplications.\n\n+ Dynamic models - how the system behaves or\nchanges when events occur.\n\n+ Process models - the business or technical\nprocesses the system must follow.\n\n+ Functional models - the hierarchy of functions\nthe system performs.",
      "fontSize": 37.80527747909167,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "+ Structural models - how the system is organized into components.\n\n+ Framework models - identify reusable architectural patterns common in similar applications.\n\n+ Dynamic models - how the system behaves or changes when events occur.\n\n+ Process models - the business or technical processes the system must follow.\n\n+ Functional models - the hierarchy of functions the system performs.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
