    {
      "id": "Hc3kN4A0S-OkxcFm_Dd9p",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 31682.96620666272,
      "y": -4665.400180578105,
      "width": 407.4790418206285,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 638456001,
      "version": 346,
      "versionNonce": 518498433,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764580955614,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "a modular, deployable, and replaceable\npart of a system that encapsulates\nimplementation and\nexposes a set of interfaces.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "a modular, deployable, and replaceable part of a system that encapsulates implementation and\nexposes a set of interfaces.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HBDQkWypZXhVnM_Q8TaV2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 32382.97470427886,
      "y": -5391.796996050448,
      "width": 788.3192138671875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1450295137,
      "version": 496,
      "versionNonce": 395105729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764583430303,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Open-Closed Principle (OCP). \n    component -> open for extension closed for modification\n\nThe Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP). \n    Subclasses should be substitutable for their base classes.\n\nDependency Inversion Principle (DIP). \n    Depend on abstractions. Do not depend on concretions.”\n\nThe Interface Segregation Principle (ISP). \n    Many client-specific interfaces are better than one general purpose interface.\n\nThe Release Reuse Equivalency Principle (REP). \n    The granule of reuse is the granule of release.”\n\nThe Common Closure Principle (CCP). \n    Classes that change together belong together.”\n\nThe Common Reuse Principle (CRP). \n    Classes that aren’t reused together should not be grouped together.”",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Open-Closed Principle (OCP). \n    component -> open for extension closed for modification\n\nThe Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP). \n    Subclasses should be substitutable for their base classes.\n\nDependency Inversion Principle (DIP). \n    Depend on abstractions. Do not depend on concretions.”\n\nThe Interface Segregation Principle (ISP). \n    Many client-specific interfaces are better than one general purpose interface.\n\nThe Release Reuse Equivalency Principle (REP). \n    The granule of reuse is the granule of release.”\n\nThe Common Closure Principle (CCP). \n    Classes that change together belong together.”\n\nThe Common Reuse Principle (CRP). \n    Classes that aren’t reused together should not be grouped together.”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
